1
00:00:00,181 --> 00:00:04,467
All right, guys. So today's video, I wanted to do another discussion video.

2
00:00:04,467 --> 00:00:07,588
Now this one is going to be headphones versus earbuds.

3
00:00:07,588 --> 00:00:13,218
Now on this channel, I've covered everything from gaming headsets to regular headphones to earbuds.

4
00:00:13,218 --> 00:00:22,761
But in the comment sections, I've always seen that I'll never use earbuds because of this, or I don't like headphones because of this, or I'll never go back to this for this reason.

5
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:28,392
So it's always got me wondering which one is actually better, or is there really a good answer for this?

6
00:00:28,392 --> 00:00:43,033
And I'll go ahead and say, there's not one specific answer, but I looked at a lot of different factors and I wanted to just kind of do a discussion just to see why one may be better than the other or which situations does one fit one better than the other.

7
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:46,180
[Design] So the first thing that I wanted to start with is design.

8
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:50,100
Now, obviously a pair of headphones, you have over the ear, you have on ear.

9
00:00:50,100 --> 00:01:00,366
And the benefits to that is it isolates you from your surroundings a lot more, but it also causes your ears to get warm and they sometimes can cause your ears to sweat.

10
00:01:00,366 --> 00:01:01,910
And a lot of people are not going to want to do that.

11
00:01:01,910 --> 00:01:05,794
And then also having a headband over your head is going to mess up your hair.

12
00:01:05,794 --> 00:01:07,294
Some people care about that.

13
00:01:07,294 --> 00:01:10,347
You may be going to work and you don't want to mess that up.

14
00:01:10,347 --> 00:01:14,313
So when you move over to look at earbuds, you have a bunch of different styles here as well.

15
00:01:14,313 --> 00:01:17,548
You have like the open air design, like regular AirPods.

16
00:01:17,548 --> 00:01:19,901
Those are made just to kind of sit in your ears...

17
00:01:19,901 --> 00:01:24,450
...or you have regular earbuds which sit in your ear canal.

18
00:01:24,450 --> 00:01:27,925
In fact, they are also using ear tips to block your ear canal.

19
00:01:27,925 --> 00:01:30,820
And that isolates you from your surroundings as well.

20
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:34,326
And there's a lot of people that can't use this type of earbud.

21
00:01:34,326 --> 00:01:35,442
They don't like ear tips.

22
00:01:35,442 --> 00:01:36,779
They don't like things in their ears.

23
00:01:36,779 --> 00:01:39,707
So that's where headphones come in.

24
00:01:39,707 --> 00:01:48,778
Now, Sony did release the LinkBuds, which is trying to create like an open-ear design where they're in your ear, but it has a ring so you can still hear your surroundings.

25
00:01:48,778 --> 00:01:50,290
I am not a huge fan of those.

26
00:01:50,290 --> 00:01:52,246
So I'm not really going to talk about that one much.

27
00:01:52,246 --> 00:01:55,044
[Portability] But I want to go ahead and move over to portability.

28
00:01:55,044 --> 00:02:01,841
Now, headphones, if you're going to take them with you, you're going to have to take a case or a pouch, or if you have your backpack, you can just throw it in that.

29
00:02:01,841 --> 00:02:05,321
So you usually have to have something extra to store those in.

30
00:02:05,321 --> 00:02:07,906
And you also are going to have to have a cable to charge them.

31
00:02:07,906 --> 00:02:12,033
Although headphones have much better battery life than earbuds do.

32
00:02:12,033 --> 00:02:16,672
But if you're taking your earbuds with you, you have the case already in your pocket.

33
00:02:16,672 --> 00:02:18,821
Now this is what also charges the earbuds.

34
00:02:18,821 --> 00:02:20,852
So that is a lot more convenient.

35
00:02:20,852 --> 00:02:23,132
And so most times you don't even need a cable.

36
00:02:23,132 --> 00:02:31,221
But most times you're not going to need a charging cable with your headphones, but just in case you are going to need to charge them, that is something extra you would have to keep up with.

37
00:02:31,221 --> 00:02:34,404
[Versatility] Now the next thing that I wanted to talk about was versatility.

38
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:41,964
Now, I've seen where a lot of companies have figured out that just having Bluetooth on a pair of earbuds doesn't really cut it.

39
00:02:41,964 --> 00:02:49,961
We've seen LG come up with an option where you can plug the charging case into another device using a three-and-a-half-millimeter headphone cable.&nbsp;

40
00:02:49,961 --> 00:02:52,771
And then it wirelessly sends your signal that way.

41
00:02:52,771 --> 00:03:03,444
Because if you're in a situation where, you know, you're on a plane and it doesn't have Bluetooth or you're in the gym and the equipment that you're on that maybe has a screen also doesn't have Bluetooth.

42
00:03:03,444 --> 00:03:08,283
It's nice to be able to plug that into that case and still be able to listen to what you're listening to.

43
00:03:08,283 --> 00:03:12,939
Where with headphones, in most cases you have that headphone cable option.

44
00:03:12,939 --> 00:03:21,880
Although there are some headphones that's just eliminated using a headphone cable altogether, but most of them, you can use a wired option if you want.

45
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:29,679
And I've also seen where a lot of companies are now realizing that all of technology is going in the direction of USB-C.

46
00:03:29,679 --> 00:03:33,627
So we've seen earbuds that have these USB-C dongles.

47
00:03:33,627 --> 00:03:47,262
This is very important for people that are going to be using their headphones or earbuds for different types of media, because this helps cut down on lag where Bluetooth devices usually still have lag, whether you notice it or not.

48
00:03:47,262 --> 00:03:49,262
And most of the time you notice it in gaming.

49
00:03:49,262 --> 00:04:00,069
Like if you're going to be shooting, you notice that slight delay with the gunshot from when you pull the trigger to when you actually hear that sound.

50
00:04:00,069 --> 00:04:03,212
That USB-C dongle does eliminate this.

51
00:04:03,212 --> 00:04:10,104
Headphones are also catching onto this because they are coming out with gaming headsets that have this USB-C dongle.

52
00:04:10,104 --> 00:04:18,708
This is mainly because the Nintendo Switch and the Steam Deck, they use a USB-C port and this eliminates any kind of lag.

53
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:25,579
And again, it just makes your device much more versatile, but both sides are realizing that this is the direction to go in.

54
00:04:25,579 --> 00:04:29,341
And I think earbuds going forward, we're going to see a lot more of those options.

55
00:04:29,341 --> 00:04:34,553
[Real world Use] And now the next category is just real-world use, how you're going to use these day to day.

56
00:04:34,553 --> 00:04:42,134
Headphones generally, again, because they're covering your ears are telling people around you, "I don't want to talk to you."

57
00:04:42,134 --> 00:04:44,105
"Don't approach me. I have headphones on." "

58
00:04:44,105 --> 00:04:46,288
Obviously I'm in my own little world.

59
00:04:46,288 --> 00:04:48,927
It is a way to just keep people from approaching...

60
00:04:48,927 --> 00:05:01,577
...where earbuds and a lot of people just use one earbud at a time allows people to listen to podcasts or music or things kind of like in the background, but still be very aware of their surroundings.

61
00:05:01,577 --> 00:05:04,638
And it also is not a turnoff for people to come talk to you.

62
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:09,891
So you would use these more so like in a work environment as you can still hear the phone.

63
00:05:09,891 --> 00:05:13,608
And if, again, if people need to get your attention, you can immediately respond.

64
00:05:13,608 --> 00:05:16,501
And the headphones, again, you can't do that. You have to pull them off.

65
00:05:16,501 --> 00:05:20,351
You can put devices in transparency or ambient mode.

66
00:05:20,351 --> 00:05:27,685
But again, for the most part, it is not the same as having one ear completely open to your surroundings.

67
00:05:27,685 --> 00:05:31,161
And it also is going to deter people from talking to you.

68
00:05:31,161 --> 00:05:36,087
So if you're at work and you have headphones on, most of the time they're going to feel like they can't approach you.

69
00:05:36,087 --> 00:05:42,837
But if I'm at home, I am definitely going to go for a pair of headphones because that's just the way that I prefer to listen to music.

70
00:05:42,837 --> 00:05:46,473
[Sound] And that leads me to the last category, which is sound.

71
00:05:46,473 --> 00:05:50,129
Now earbuds have come a long way from when they were first released.

72
00:05:50,129 --> 00:05:51,727
The technology has gotten better.

73
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:53,442
The Bluetooth codecs are getting better.

74
00:05:53,442 --> 00:05:56,324
We're seeing LDAC, we're seeing high-res audio.

75
00:05:56,324 --> 00:06:00,429
It is definitely going in the right direction when it comes to audio quality...

76
00:06:00,429 --> 00:06:12,780
...but I still do not think that it is going to top sitting down at my desk at home, plugged into an amp with a wired pair of studio headphones that I'm able to hear a lot more things.

77
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:17,807
I'm able to get a lot more space, especially because I prefer using open-back headphones.

78
00:06:17,807 --> 00:06:23,681
And that type of experience hasn't been replicated in a pair of earbuds yet.

79
00:06:23,681 --> 00:06:31,863
And earbuds, if you're a bass head, they haven't found anything to replicate like the Skullcandy Crushers yet where you have that haptic feedback.

80
00:06:31,863 --> 00:06:33,863
There's a lot of options on both sides.

81
00:06:33,863 --> 00:06:36,569
I do see that earbuds are outselling headphones.

82
00:06:36,569 --> 00:06:42,022
I do think that people are going more for the portability and the convenience factor of earbuds.

83
00:06:42,022 --> 00:06:43,684
Headphones are cumbersome.

84
00:06:43,684 --> 00:06:44,867
They take up space.

85
00:06:44,867 --> 00:06:47,909
They're just, again, not as portable as a pair of earbuds.

86
00:06:47,909 --> 00:06:52,387
But earbuds just still cannot replicate the sound of headphones.

87
00:06:52,387 --> 00:06:54,850
And I think it's still going to come down to personal preference.

88
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:59,741
Again, I like the fact that I can kind of use either depending on what my situation is...

89
00:06:59,741 --> 00:07:01,737
...but I do love the sound of headphones.

90
00:07:01,737 --> 00:07:04,486
I kind of generally lean in that direction.

91
00:07:04,486 --> 00:07:08,745
So it's got me wondering, what do you guys prefer and why?

92
00:07:08,745 --> 00:07:10,814
Like, why would you go with a pair of earbuds?

93
00:07:10,814 --> 00:07:15,075
Why would you go with a pair of headphones and why do you like one over the other?

94
00:07:15,075 --> 00:07:17,687
I mean, everybody has their own personal tastes.

95
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:20,853
So I'm actually curious as to what you prefer...

96
00:07:20,853 --> 00:07:23,420
...but this is my reasoning between each device.

97
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:25,599
It's at least different ways to look at these.

98
00:07:25,599 --> 00:07:27,882
And I thought it would be a good thing to discuss here.

99
00:07:27,882 --> 00:07:33,649
But guys, that wraps up my video on my discussion with the headphones versus earbuds.

100
00:07:33,649 --> 00:07:35,764
Thank you so much for checking out this video.

101
00:07:35,764 --> 00:07:38,632
Thank you so much for checking out all the other videos...

102
00:07:38,632 --> 00:07:41,132
...and as always, make sure to stay tuned for more.

